            "value": "The formation of KHG is inhibited by halides and substrate analogs such as hydroxypyruvate, tartrate, oxalate or acetaldehyde (PubMed:7016177). KHG aldolase activity is also inhibited by bromopyruvate, which specifically esterifies Glu-45 (PubMed:1978721). Activity is partially inhibited by p-mercuriphenylsulfonate, iodoacetate and N-ethylmaleimide (PubMed:4560498)"
